{"name":"Regal View","hex":"#749e8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or suitable for royalty.","Befitting a monarch.\n\n Befitting a king or emperor."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, portable organ whose sound is produced by brass beating reeds without amplifying resonators. Its tone is keen and rich in harmonics. The regal was common in the 16th and 17th centuries, and has been revived for the performance of music from those times.","An organ stop of the reed family, furnished with a normal beating reed, but whose resonator is a fraction of its natural length. In the 16th and 17th centuries these stops took a multitude of forms. Today only one survives that is of universal currency, the so-called vox humana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regal"},{"term":"view","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Visual perception.\nThe act of seeing or looking at something.","The act of seeing or looking at something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look at.","To regard in a stated way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"regal":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-regal.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-regal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-regal.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-regal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-regal.wav.ogg"}],"view":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-view.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm